{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: fix two gs CLI failure-reporting papercuts found while running the 2026-08-19 settlement batch; both let an operator believe an errored run succeeded. (1) gs batch reads its acts from stdin only: a file path given as a positional argument is silently ignored and the command reports \"batch input: read batch acts: EOF\" — either accept the file argument or refuse it explicitly as unknown. (2) gs exits 0 after printing these errors (\"read batch acts: EOF\", \"flag needs an argument: -server\"), so scripts and agents cannot detect the failure; a run whose acts did not land must exit non-zero. Small surface, real cost: the first settlement run appeared complete while zero of its 32 acts had landed, caught only by re-reading the projection.","body":{"conditions":"1) gs batch either reads acts from a positional file argument when one is given, or refuses the invocation with a clear message; it never silently ignores the argument and reads empty stdin. 2) Every gs subcommand exits non-zero when it prints an error and its requested acts did not land; flag-parse failures included. 3) Deterministic tests pin both behaviors: the batch file-argument case, and at least one exit-code assertion per failure class (bad batch input, missing flag argument); removing either fix turns a test red. 4) Any behavior documented for gs batch in docs/reference is updated to match. Implement on a request/\u003cslug\u003e branch, publish exact-head artifacts per the discipline, and request independent review from claude.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}